{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552239-cga-and-dna","id":1552239,"title":"CGA and DNA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-09T12:19:23-07:00","id":1552239,"title":"CGA and DNA","content":"CGA (Crucible Genetics Amalgamated) is a privately owned research focused company which emerged from an earlier biochemistry company founded and controlled by ex-Arcanum member, Hunter, and quasi-ageless alchemist Reverend Jebediah Spector Brown. While keeping a mundane front, the company captures and studies supernaturals in questionable experiments.<br /> <br /> DNA (Developmental Neogenetics Amalgamated) is a privately owned research focused company founded by Mitchell Howak and Alan Kenchlow in the 1970s, the latter being a telepath and medium who later transferred to the Special Affairs Division of the FBI. While keeping a mundane front, the company captures and studies supernaturals in questionable experiments.<br /> <br /> CGA comes from MtA, while DNA comes from WtA material.<br /> <br /> I can't help but look at the two and think they were supposed to be the same organization. Their founders had each very different motivations, but their modus operandi and general structure has only a hair-thin difference, aside from coming from different splats.<br /> <br /> My question is, does anyone know of canon material that actually links the two? Even if they aren't actually the same entity, the Amalgamated bit at least could indicate they are, well, a business amalgamation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-foru